  "commemorates": "American's centennial (2026), in the look of its first DC-3 Flagships (1936).",
  "description": "Fuselage: light silver-gray all over with a red radome; a thin red cheatline along the windows' foot, nose to tail, stepped twice like a lightning bolt behind the cockpit. Titles: 'AMERICAN AIRLINES' in navy capitals between the steps; the Flagship pennant and 'THE Flagship' in a navy script, underlined, over the windows ahead of the wing; 'AMERICAN' over the 1930s AA eagle roundel (a navy disc, the red A's either side of a white eagle) aft. Tail: silver fin with a red band down the trailing edge. Engines silver with a red front and a small red arrow.",
